Oryn on FreeBSD: after installing
=================================

Required: nothing beyond the base system. Everything below is optional and
adds readings.

1. CPU temperatures: load the sensor driver (AMD: amdtemp, Intel: coretemp)

     sudo kldload amdtemp                  # or: coretemp
     sudo sysrc kld_list+="amdtemp"        # keep it after reboot

2. CPU power (watts), RAM temperatures and part numbers: two more kernel
   modules (read as root)

     sudo kldload cpuctl smb
     sudo sysrc kld_list+="cpuctl smb"

3. Optional packages

     sudo pkg install smartmontools        # SATA/NVMe SMART temperatures
     sudo pkg install dmidecode            # RAM model and speed without root
     sudo pkg install nvidia-driver        # NVIDIA GPU panel (nvidia-smi)

4. Run it

     oryn              # everything readable as a normal user
     sudo oryn         # adds SMART, CPU watts, RAM, NVMe health and
                       # NVIDIA hotspot / VRAM temperatures

   Optional: let a normal `oryn` use smartctl and dmidecode without a
   password (Oryn only ever runs them with `sudo -n`, never asks):

     echo "$USER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/smartctl, /usr/local/sbin/dmidecode" \
       | sudo tee /usr/local/etc/sudoers.d/oryn
     sudo chmod 440 /usr/local/etc/sudoers.d/oryn

Check what was found:  oryn --list
Manual:                man oryn
